Hoshi is the part that builds a bundle, installs it, sends documents to the
translation engines, keeps a record of how each translation was made and
warns when one looks as if it dropped text. It translates nothing itself.
The translating is done by other people's work, which Hoshi fetches when a
bundle is built and carries inside the bundle unchanged. This file says
whose work that is and on what terms it is passed on.

Hoshi is built from LibreTranslate's open source software. Hoshi is not
officially associated with LibreTranslate or its products. Nor is it
associated with, or endorsed by, Argos Open Technologies, Ollama, Google,
Docker or the Wikimedia Foundation.

